<div class="dialogue">"Oye Kavya, bathroom khali hai."<span class="gloss-en">Hey Kavya, the bathroom's free.</span></div>

You nearly walk into the wall. Your eyes are physically incapable of not registering: a nearly-naked woman, three feet away, no screen mediating. But the body doesn't respond the way yours would   no rush of blood southward, because there's nowhere for it to rush. Instead: a warmth in the lower abdomen. Diffuse. Confusing.

"Haan, thanks," you manage, walking sideways.

Another girl passes in a thin nightie, braless. <div class="dialogue">"Hi Kavya."</div> Gone.

Kavya wouldn't bat an eye. Three years of shared showers and borrowed bras. The female body is her default, her unremarkable. You keep your eyes forward. Don't look. //Don't look.//
