:: meera_reunion_d3
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">Reunion</span>
<<img "meera_reunion.png" "Room 304, six months ending">>
She's on her bed. White kurta, loose hair, no makeup, exactly like every photo you've memorised except real   three-dimensional, breathing, the kajal slightly smudged from sleep. She's biting her lower lip, a nervous habit photos don't capture.

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun?"</div>

You nod. Kavya's throat has sealed shut.

Then the tears come   fast, faster than any tears you've ever produced. Your male body needs a buildup, an emotional levy overtopping. Kavya's body has no delay. The emotion registers and the ducts respond instantly.

"Main yahan hoon," you say. The words crack in the middle.<span class="gloss-en">I'm here.</span>

And then you're holding each other   your small arms around her back, her face in Kavya's hair. Six months of absence compressed into a collision of borrowed skin and real souls. You're shorter now; your face presses to her shoulder instead of the top of her head. The geometry has inverted. She's holding //you//.

<div class="dialogue">"Your eyes."</div>

Her hands cup Kavya's face, the beauty mark under her thumb.

<div class="dialogue">"The rest is Kavya but the eyes   that's Arjun."</div>

She looks into Kavya's dark eyes and sees you. Love doesn't follow the rules of optics.

Ten minutes. Priya's alarm hasn't gone off yet.
