Meera spreads the palm leaves in sequence on her bed. Her translation notebook   Sanskrit to Hindi, English annotations, dancer's penmanship.

"This reads like a system architecture document," you say. "The ritual section's the API. The theory's the documentation. And the warnings   "

<div class="dialogue">"The warnings are the error-handling."</div>

You grin. Kavya's grin, which you're told is rare and worth seeing. Two hours. Sections numbered, cross-referenced, warnings in red ink. The intersection of her Sanskrit and your systems thinking.

<div class="dialogue">"You're different in her body. Softer. When you look at me, Kavya looks at me like a friend she's protecting. You look at me like I'm the only thing in the room."</div>

