:: anatomy_horror_d3
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">Survival</span>
<<img "arjun_anatomy_horror.png" "the dissection hall">>
The formalin hits Kavya's olfactory system like a chemical weapon deployed against civilians. Your male nose endured it in the abstract. This nose //amplifies// it   sharper, more invasive, coating the inside of your nostrils.

You gag. Openly, loudly, doubling forward. Sneha pats your back.

<div class="dialogue">"Kavya, teesre saal mein bhi? Tu badal nahi rahi."<span class="gloss-en">Still, in third year? You never change.</span></div>

You haven't changed. You've been replaced. But the nausea is genuine, and Kavya's zero-latency tear ducts interpret the formalin as emotional stimulus and produce tears at a rate your body reserves for actual grief.

Dr. Sharma: <div class="dialogue">"Thoracic cavity review. Continue your dissections."</div>

You pick up the scalpel. Kavya's hand is steady   the motor cortex remembers this even as your mind recoils. When you stop thinking and let her hand do what it knows, the blade moves with precision along the intercostal space. You understand maybe thirty percent of what you're seeing. Enough to know the stringy white things are nerves.

Meera, three rows ahead, makes a tiny thumbs-up. You return it and feel the breasts shift as you raise your arm. Even a thumbs-up involves breasts in this body. Everything does.

Two hours. You survive them.
</div>\
<<run setup.flag("in_dissection_d3")>>\
<<run setup.flag("anatomy_done_d3")>>\
