<<img "room_304_arjun_pov.png" "the terrace, evening light">>
Alone. Finally. Under the sky, in a body she doesn't recognise but eyes she does.

Her thumb traces your jaw   Kavya's jaw, softer, rounder. Your breath catches, Kavya's smaller lungs managing less air. Six months you've imagined this, except in every imagination you were in your own body, your own height, your own lips.

These aren't your lips. They're Kavya's. If you kiss Meera now it's two women's faces pressing together. The geometry is different. Everything is different except the want, which is yours, which doesn't care what body it's housed in.

